stateDiagram-v2
    %% CURRENT implementation; sources and guards in transition inventory.
    state "issued (derived: admitted_at null)" as issued
    state "admitted (derived)" as admitted
    state "authentication evidence recorded (derived)" as evidence
    state "revoked_at present" as revoked
    state "completed_at present" as completed
    state "cancelled_at present" as cancelled
    [*] --> issued
    [*] --> admitted
    issued --> admitted: admit!
    admitted --> evidence: record_authentication_evidence!
    issued --> revoked: revoke! / rotate_and_admit! previous row
    issued --> issued: rotate! same row
    admitted --> revoked: revoke! / rotate_and_admit! previous row
    admitted --> admitted: rotate! same row
    evidence --> revoked: revoke! / rotate_and_admit! previous row
    evidence --> evidence: rotate! same row
    admitted --> completed: complete!
    admitted --> cancelled: cancel!
    evidence --> completed: complete!
    evidence --> cancelled: cancel!
    revoked --> [*]
    completed --> [*]
    cancelled --> [*]
    note right of issued
        Labels are derived, not stored state strings.
        TTL expiry makes active? false without a state write.
        rotate_and_admit! starts a replacement row admitted.
    end note
